## 9. Risks and open questions

| Item | Why it matters | What to do |
|---|---|---|
| Original slope algorithm unknown | We match within 0.2° but cannot claim it is identical | State it plainly in the docs |
| Surface model includes canopy | Slope in forest is noisy | List under limitations |
| Coverage limited to areas near 7 capitals | Model has no basis elsewhere | Restrict the map; do not show Sikkim |
| Only 20 random zones in the first run | Slope choice not confirmed on typical terrain | Rerun with 200 |
| 22 zones have interpolated training slope | Their training values are less reliable | Prefer DEM values for them going forward |
| Data provenance not yet written down | The PRD requires it | Fill `provenance.json` early, including which data is real or simulated |
| Land cover is not a model input | It can only appear on the map for now | Say so; retraining with it is a future extension |
| Cloud cover in Sentinel imagery | Monsoon gaps | Use dry-season composites |
| Which Copernicus release | Release differences would be tiny | We matched the AWS bucket to millimetres, so use that source |

